{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954203-weapons-for-the-supernaturally-strong-and-fast","id":954203,"title":"Weapons for the Supernaturally strong and fast.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-19T21:53:45-07:00","id":954203,"title":"Weapons for the Supernaturally strong and fast.","content":"So if you have millions of dollars, maybe access to billions, wouldn't you be able to design high grade weapons to take advantage of the fact you can lift and bare more then average joe mortal? The regular go to example is the Chaingun, or the guns in Hellsing and Gungrave.<br /> <br /> Would it be fair to say modify the template of the high end weapons we have stats for like ruger redhawk, in the revised Vampire companion one of the best resources for equipment. But how would you beef things up?<br /> <br /> Probably the easiest weapons to design would be Melee.<br /> <br /> What about Armor? How beefy could you get armor if you are strong enough to wear it, or have special powers that allow you to negate the bad effects?<br /> <br /> For Vampires they could have combo disciplines to do things like ignore the knock back to rapid fire a gun, or a fan fire pistol. Shifters can make things into fetishes to remove penalties and give unique abilities to the equipment. And Mages can do insane stuff with even basic powers.<br /> <br /> Thoughts and assistance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T19:12:21-07:00","id":954738,"title":"","content":"Not really all that much for mundane weapons, in pure mechanics terms. You can get insane pistols that fire .50 BMG rounds, but that would do less damage than a machine gun with the same cartridge and have a substantially truncated range. At some point, the insanity is also too great; trying to use, say, a GAU-8 Avenger taken off its mount, you'd have to contend with the fact that it's powerful enough to interfere with the forward motion of an A-10, which has an empty weight of around ten metric tons. Only Mokole have the bulk to really use something like that in a totally unconventional, off-the-wall game of oversized personal weapons. Also, all that DU ammo is going to be a bitch to buy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T01:31:11-07:00","id":954884,"title":"","content":"I play Werewolf most often so I am gonna talk about that. The sky is the limit as far as fetishes are concerned, you just need to be good at craftsmanship and negotiating (or browbeating, but for Garou the difference is often moot). Generally I like the idea of fetishes being made out of things that hold importance to the creator, rather than being state-of-the-art Weaver junk. A Bone Gnawer forging a glass dagger out of shards from a window of the tenement she grew up in seems more interesting to me than an oversized titanium alloy katana. <br /> <br /> By the way, even if you can lift a weapon that is the size of a buster sword, it still impractical. E.G. Grand Klaives are cool but they are awkward to use, which is reflected by a higher difficulty... and if you have friends or packmates anywhere close at hand, your botches will likely have horrific results.<br /> <br /> Armor for werewolves seems almost unnecessary, given their natural regeneration, ability to soak aggro, and the availability of gifts that increase soak pools; that said, I have given some NPCs fetish armor, the extra protection comes in handy when storming the hellish maws of Thunder Wyrms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T09:14:26-07:00","id":954973,"title":"","content":"Isn't there something in a dark ages vampire book about potence forged weapons and armor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T06:38:30-07:00","id":967284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954203-weapons-for-the-supernaturally-strong-and-fast?p=954973#post954973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't there something in a dark ages vampire book about potence forged weapons and armor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, also blood tempering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/398-rat_bastard","name":"rat_bastard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar398_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T19:24:14-07:00","id":1141994,"title":"","content":"One of the Potence 6 powers (Master of the Forge) allows you to forge better weapons and armour. Mostly, it makes the weapons do +1 damage and be immune to being destroyed by using them with the exceptional strength the wielder would apply.<br /> Vampires with exceptional Craft Skill (6+) Could possibly design better weapons too, but even with great strength, the leverage issues with an oversized weapon still exist.<br /> The best enhancement to weapons for damage would be the benefits of sorcery enhancement - the fetish benefits, Thaumaturgy and Necromancy etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}